                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>Baron de Beust to Mr.
                        Motley.</head>
                <p>The undersigned, minister of the imperial household and of foreign affairs, has
                    hastened to lay before the Emperor, his most gracious master, the note which the
                    honorable envoy of the United States, Mr. J. Lothrop Motley, under instructions
                    from his government, was so obliging as to address to him in regard to the
                    flagitious attempt brought to notice during the latest visit of his imperial
                    royal apostolic Majesty in Prague.</p>
                <p>Hereupon his Majesty has been pleased to command the undersigned most
                    respectfully to request the envoy kindly to inform the President of the United
                    States, that although the judicial investigation instituted in regard to the
                    said occurrence has not yet resulted in a confirmation of the grave accusation
                    raised, still the proof of friendly sympathy offered on this occasion by the
                    President of the United States to his Majesty has been received by him with the
                    heartiest thanks.</p>
                <p>The undersigned profits by this occasion to renew to the envoy the assurance of
                    his most distinguished consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>BEUST.</signed>
                    <lb/>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >VIENNA</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1866-12-23"><hi rendition="#italic">December</hi> 23,
                        1866</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
